Subject: [PATCH 11/11] geph5-app: follow GEPH5_STATE_DIR for state and runtime dirs on Linux

The engine side of patch 0010. state_dir() and runtime_dir() are what pick
settings.json, the cache, manager.log and the engine/engine.sock IPC socket;
on Linux all of them were rooted at /var/lib/geph and /run/geph, which belong
to the official install. A side-by-side install (Linux port of the Termux
deployment model) now redirects the whole cluster under $GEPH5_STATE_DIR,
exactly like the Android arm routes everything through android_state_dir():
same variable, same precedence (override, then platform default), and the
engine socket lands in $GEPH5_STATE_DIR/run so two managers' engines never
collide.

Ports are deliberately NOT touched here: SOCKS5/HTTP listen ports live in
settings.json (proxy.socks5_port / proxy.http_port, seeded by the installer)
and the PAC port follows GEPH5_PAC_PORT from patch 0008 — that trio is the
documented side-by-side port shift (9929/9930/12233).

Defaults are byte-identical with the variable unset. Fragility: low — the
diff is an additive cfg arm in each resolver; it conflicts only if upstream
reworks the path constants, which patch 0006 would report first anyway.

Deliberately not done: no attempt to segregate the VPN-plane globals (nft
table `geph`, TUN_IFACE, ip rules) — two installs are expected to run proxy
mode only; full-tunnel on both would fight over the kill switch regardless
of paths.
